// @name: 02 — Strudel + Hydra
// @tagline: audio + visuals synced on the shared clock
// @description: One self-contained `.bps`: a Strudel actor (→ audio) and a Hydra actor (→ video), both inlined as backticks on the same transport. The Hydra patch reads `beat` and `bar` from the shared clock to pulse in time. Ctrl+Enter to evaluate; one Ctrl+. hushes both.
// @language: strudel
// @outputs: audio, visual
// @level: intermediate
// @tags: sync, visuals
// @showcase
//
// 02 — Strudel + Hydra synchronisés sur le transport Kanopi (migré de 02-strudel-hydra.kanopi).
// Deux voix de code : Strudel → audio, Hydra → vidéo. `beat`/`bar` sont injectés par
// l'adaptateur Hydra de Kanopi (horloge partagée, cf. ADAPTER_SPEC §5bis).

core

actor groove  eval.strudel
actor viz  eval.hydra

-----
S -> { groove_r, viz_r }

groove_r -> groove.`stack(
  note("c2*4").s("sawtooth").gain(0.5),
  note("c5*8").s("square").gain(0.2)
)`

viz_r -> viz.`osc(60, 0.1, () => 0.5 + 0.5 * Math.sin(beat * Math.PI))
  .rotate(() => bar * 0.05)
  .out()`
